---
import { ENTITY } from '../config';

const SCIENCE = [
  {
    title: 'A semi-enclosed bay with a working intertidal zone',
    tag: 'Semi-enclosed bay & intertidal flat',
    text: 'Manila Bay is a shallow, semi-enclosed bay opening to the South China Sea, with slow water exchange. At low tide the exposed intertidal flat is habitat for crabs, shellfish and polychaetes, and an important feeding ground for migratory waterbirds.',
  },
  {
    title: 'A stopover on the East Asian–Australasian Flyway',
    tag: 'East Asian–Australasian Flyway',
    text: 'The Las Piñas–Parañaque critical habitat on the bay\'s south side is a key stopover on the flyway; large flocks of waders and egrets are seen roughly November to March. Keep your distance and do not enter closed areas.',
  },
  {
    title: 'The Dolomite Beach is engineered nourishment, not a natural beach',
    tag: 'Engineered nourishment, not natural sand',
    text: 'Dolomite Beach is a beach-nourishment project: crushed dolomite replaces eroded shoreline to stabilise the coast and restore public space. It is not a natural beach, and its upkeep needs continuous investment — hence the no-plastic, no-swimming rules.',
  },
];

const RESPONSIBILITIES = [
  'Take your trash with you: boardwalk bins overflow at peak times, so bring your own bag',
  'Respect the single-use plastic limits: stow plastic bottles, wrappers and straws before the beach, use reusables',
  'Do not feed, collect or catch: birds and intertidal life are very sensitive to human disturbance',
  'Do not swim: the bay is still under rehabilitation and both water quality and the underwater terrain are unsuitable',
  'Respect residents and other visitors: it is a shared space — keep noise down and do not block the walkway',
  'Use drones cautiously: launches may be restricted on site and can disturb birds',
  'Prefer low-carbon arrival: rail, walking and ride-sharing ease crowd and emission pressure on the bay',
];
---
<section id="stewardship" class="anchor-offset py-16 sm:py-20 md:py-24">
  <div class="container-wide">
    <div class="max-w-3xl mb-10">
      <span class="chip bg-palm-green/10 text-palm-green mb-4">Science &amp; responsibility</span>
      <h2 class="section-title">Understand the bay, then leave it better</h2>
      <p class="section-subtitle mb-0">
        Why there are no-plastic and no-swimming rules, why the sand is white, and why the bay is worth protecting — understanding the science behind it matters more than memorising the rules.
      </p>
    </div>

    <div class="grid lg:grid-cols-3 gap-6 mb-8">
      {
        SCIENCE.map((s, i) => (
          <article class="card p-6 flex flex-col">
            <div class="flex items-center gap-2 mb-3">
              <span class="w-7 h-7 rounded-lg bg-palm-green/10 text-palm-green text-xs font-semibold flex items-center justify-center">
                {i + 1}
              </span>
              <span class="chip bg-sand-warm text-ocean-mid text-[11px]">{s.tag}</span>
            </div>
            <h3 class="font-display text-lg font-semibold text-ocean-deep mb-2 leading-snug">{s.title}</h3>
            <p class="text-sm text-ocean-mid leading-relaxed flex-1">{s.text}</p>
          </article>
        ))
      }
    </div>

    <div class="grid lg:grid-cols-5 gap-6">
      <div class="lg:col-span-2 card p-6 sm:p-7 border-sunset-orange/20">
        <h3 class="font-display text-lg font-semibold text-ocean-deep mb-3">Water quality &amp; swimming</h3>
        <p class="text-sm text-ocean-mid leading-relaxed mb-4">
          Manila Bay rehabilitation is a long-term effort, and water quality shifts with rain, runoff and tides. Never judge safety by how the water looks on a clear day — whether contact is allowed follows the authorities and on-site notices; swimming is currently banned on the beach.
        </p>
        <ul class="space-y-2 text-sm text-ocean-mid leading-relaxed">
          <li class="flex gap-2"><span class="text-sunset-orange">▸</span> Turbidity usually rises noticeably within 24 – 48 h after rain</li>
          <li class="flex gap-2"><span class="text-sunset-orange">▸</span> Wash children's hands with clean water and soap after playing in the sand</li>
          <li class="flex gap-2"><span class="text-sunset-orange">▸</span> If there is an odour or a warning line, follow on-site staff guidance</li>
        </ul>
      </div>

      <div class="lg:col-span-3 card p-6 sm:p-7">
        <h3 class="font-display text-lg font-semibold text-ocean-deep mb-4">Visitor responsibility</h3>
        <ol class="space-y-3">
          {
            RESPONSIBILITIES.map((r, i) => (
              <li class="flex gap-3 text-sm text-ocean-mid leading-relaxed">
                <span class="shrink-0 w-6 h-6 rounded-lg bg-sand-warm text-ocean-deep text-xs font-semibold flex items-center justify-center mt-0.5">
                  {i + 1}
                </span>
                <span>{r}</span>
              </li>
            ))
          }
        </ol>
        <p class="mt-5 pt-4 border-t border-sand-warm text-xs text-ocean-mid/85 leading-relaxed">
          Ecology and rehabilitation progress follow the agencies' public data:
          <a href={ENTITY.denrUrl} target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="text-sunset-orange hover:underline mx-1">DENR</a>·
          <a href={ENTITY.cityGovUrl} target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="text-sunset-orange hover:underline mx-1">City of Manila</a>·
          <a href={ENTITY.govtTourismUrl} target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="text-sunset-orange hover:underline mx-1">Department of Tourism</a>.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>
